<title>HONG KONG: China Merchant Hai Hong H1 net up 105 pct.</title>
<headline>China Merchant Hai Hong H1 net up 105 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   13.82	vs 6.73</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    2.0	  vs 3.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  54.86 gain vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    97.57	vs 47.52</p>
<p>    Turnover		     360.80     vs 384.08</p>
<p>    Company name		 China Merchants Hai Hong Holdings</p>
<p>				     Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  October 8-11</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 18</p>
<p>NOTE - China Merchants Hai Hong is a paint manufacturer.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of a 4.95 percent interest in Ming Wah Universal (Bermuda) Co Ltd and the dilution of the group's shareholding to 75 percent of the enlarged issued share capital of Ming Wah, following the listing of the shares of Ming Wah, which owns and operates a fleet of vessels, on the Singapore Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
